## Story Description
Update dashboard/app.py to use client_config.py for branding and to show a professional homepage. The current homepage shows 3 bare metrics and a bullet list with a 'Procurement analytics pipeline' heading. Replace this with: (1) client name + engagement title as the page header, (2) data freshness badge, (3) the 3 KPI metrics, (4) a professional navigation guide. Remove all developer-facing language from error/info messages.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — add import: from dashboard.client_config import get_client_name, get_engagement_title, get_currency_label, get_data_freshness
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — update st.set_page_config: change page_title to use a dynamic value. Use: title = get_engagement_title(); if get_client_name(): title = f"{get_client_name()} — {title}"; st.set_page_config(page_title=title, page_icon='📊', layout='wide', initial_sidebar_bar='expanded'). Note: page_icon changes from 💰 to 📊.
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — in main(), replace st.title('SpendCube — Procurement Analytics') with: client = get_client_name(); title = get_engagement_title(); if client: st.title(f'{client}'); st.subheader(title); else: st.title(title). Then add immediately after: freshness = get_data_freshness(); st.caption(f'Data last refreshed: {freshness}').
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — replace the error message in load_cube_data() that says 'Run `make build-cube`...' with: st.error('Spend data not yet loaded. Please contact your analyst to refresh the dataset.')
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — in main(), replace the st.info() no-data message that shows 'make ingest && make harmonise...' with: st.info('No spend data found. Please contact your analyst to load a dataset.')
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — replace the st.markdown 'Procurement spend analytics pipeline. Use the sidebar...' line with: st.markdown('Use the sidebar to navigate between analysis views.')
- Edit file: dashboard/app.py — update the navigation list markdown to replace internal names with client-appropriate descriptions: Spend Overview = 'KPIs, monthly trend, category and supplier breakdown', Category Deep Dive = 'Category drill-down from L1 to L3, supplier fragmentation, savings signals', Supplier Deep Dive = 'Per-supplier spend profile, payment terms benchmark, risk flags', Payment Terms = 'Working capital opportunity, terms distribution, supplier benchmark'. Remove Data Quality and Review Workstation from this list — they are internal.
- Run: PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) python3 -m py_compile dashboard/app.py && echo 'syntax OK'

